From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meanaverage <18336095+meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:48:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(connector): answer Auto-Detect Requests that come after
 the connect-time phase

Windows Server with RDS licensing sends Auto-Detect Requests on the MCS
message channel in the middle of the licensing exchange, which runs to
its full length there, and again while it prepares the Demand Active.
The connector answered them only in its connect-time auto-detection
phase, which the first licensing PDU ends; every later phase handed
whatever arrived to its own decoder, and the licensing header's
"invalid security header flags" ended the connection before the session
opened. A host without licensing ends the exchange with one error
message, which is why it was not affected.

The phases from licensing to connection finalization now tell a message
channel PDU from the I/O channel PDU they wait for. An Auto-Detect
Request is answered as during the connect-time phase, which is what
mstsc and FreeRDP do (FreeRDP's licensing step notes the same of
Windows Server 2012 R2 and 2019); anything else on the message channel
is ignored; and the phase goes on waiting. The multitransport
bootstrapping phase, which already routes by channel, answers them too,
without counting them as multitransport requests.

Upstream: Devolutions/IronRDP#1629.
